KEY TO LEFT JOINS IS WHICH COLUMN DO WE WANT TO KEEP ALL OF THE DATA? THAT IS THE PRIMARY TABLE WE DRAW FROM (LEFT TABLE). 
(What should every row in my final row represent?)(If it's about buildings, start w buildings, if it's about employees start w employees)
LEFT JOIN RIGHT TABLE WITH DATA YOU WOULD NOT CARE TO KEEP


If you only need matching records use an inner join
If you have 1 table as a primary source and want to add into that, use a left join
If you need every record from both tables use a FULL JOIN

Select query with constraints on NULL values
